      ],
      "source": "https://cityofnewdale.org/our-history"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "On June 27, 1914, the Oregon Short Line Railroad bought a right of way from Sam and Fred Schwendiman to lay tracks near Newdale.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newdale%2C_Idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlers in Newdale included families such as Siddoway, Briggs, and Schwendiman.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newdale%2C_Idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The community center opened in June 1915, drawing considerable attention from residents and visitors alike.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newdale%2C_Idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Newdale completed its water system on March 17, 1916, featuring a wooden elevated tank and underground mains.",
